# Detection Checklist

Every dimension here is a genuine fork: CakePHP offers two or more valid approaches, the app's choice changes what the next agent writes, and no tool can pick for you. Left out on purpose: pure formatting (PHPCS owns it), any form Rector/PHPStan rewrites to one canonical shape, and framework defaults any agent writes unprompted (Bake Table/Entity pairs, `fetchTable()`, PSR-12).

Each item gives the fork, then a hint (a grep or dir to spot which side the app takes). Hints are only a start. Read the matched files, never record on a raw count. Apply the ground rules to every verdict: a consistent choice that is a default or a tool's target form is not a pattern. Rows tagged (architecture) are the highest-signal, so record presence and deliberate absence.

---

## A. Validation & HTTP input

1. Validation entry point: Table `validationDefault()` / `validation*()` vs `src/Form` classes vs `$this->request->getData()` checks in controllers.
   - Hint: `ls src/Form`; grep -- `validationDefault`, `->getData(` in controllers vs Tables.
2. Custom rule location: Table/provider rules vs invokable validators vs inline closures.
   - Hint: grep `add(` / `Provider` in Tables; look for dedicated validator classes.
3. Typed / filtered retrieval: `$this->request->getQuery()` / `getData()` with casts vs raw array access.
   - Hint: grep `getQuery(`, `getData(`, `getParam(` density in `src/Controller`.
4. Custom messages/attributes: `resources/locales/*/validation.php` (or `resources/locales`) vs Form/`Validator` message maps.
   - Hint: `ls resources/locales`; grep -- `->set*` message APIs in Forms/Tables.

## B. Controllers & routing

5. Controller shape: thin actions vs multi-method CRUD vs dedicated action classes.
   - Hint: read a few controllers; count lines per action; `ls src/Controller`.
6. Business-logic location (architecture): fat controllers vs delegated to Services / Tables / Commands / Jobs.
   - Hint: read a few controller methods; `ls src/Service src/Services`.
7. Route style: `config/routes.php` named routes vs array URLs vs plugin routes only.
   - Hint: grep `_name`, `Router::url` vs array `['controller' =>` usage.
8. Middleware assignment: `Application` / plugin middleware queue vs controller-level checks.
   - Hint: grep `middleware(` in `Application.php` / plugins vs auth checks in controllers.
9. Entity loading: `get()` / `getAssociation` / `contain` in controllers vs Table finder methods.
   - Hint: grep -- `->get(`, `->find(`, `contain(` in controllers vs Tables.
10. CSRF / form protection: framework defaults vs custom skips / token helpers.
    - Hint: grep `CsrfProtection`, `FormProtection`, `unlockedFields`.

## C. Authorization

11. Authorization home: Authorization plugin Policy classes vs AuthComponent / custom gates vs middleware-only.
    - Hint: `ls src/Policy`; grep `can*`, `Authorization` in `src/`.
12. Authorization call site: `$this->Authorization->authorize()` / `can()` vs manual checks in controllers.
    - Hint: grep -- `Authorization`, `->can(`, `authorize(` in controllers.

## D. Tables, entities & ORM

13. Mass assignment: entity `$_accessible` whitelist (`'*' => false`) vs open `'*' => true`.
    - Hint: grep `$_accessible` in `src/Model/Entity`.
14. Virtual / computed fields: `_getXxx` / `_setXxx` vs dedicated presenters / view vars only.
    - Hint: grep `function _get`, `function _set`, `$_virtual` in entities.
15. Primary keys: auto-increment integers vs UUIDs / ULIDs.
    - Hint: grep `uuid`, `Uuid`, `BinaryUuid` in migrations and entities.
16. Custom types / marshaling: custom `Type` classes vs inline casting in entities.
    - Hint: `ls src/Database/Type`; grep `Type::map`, `$_cast` patterns.
17. Data/query layer (architecture): Tables queried in controllers vs repositories vs rich Table finders.
    - Hint: `ls src/Repository src/Query`; see where non-trivial queries are built.
18. Finder methods: `findXxx` on Tables vs ad-hoc `where` chains in callers.
    - Hint: grep `function find` in Tables; compare caller style.
19. Model events / callbacks: Table `beforeSave`/`afterSave` vs listeners vs application events.
    - Hint: grep `beforeSave`, `afterSave`, `EventManager` in `src/Model`.
20. Contain / select posture: per-query `contain`/`select` vs default associations always loaded.
    - Hint: grep `contain(`, `select(` density in Tables vs controllers.

## E. Architecture & organization

21. Service structure (architecture): Service classes (constructor-injected) vs fat Tables vs neither. Cross-check the Step 0 `src/` map.
    - Hint: `ls src/` (whole tree); grep how Services are constructed/called.
22. Forms / DTOs (architecture): `src/Form` vs plain arrays vs readonly DTO classes.
    - Hint: `ls src/Form src/Dto src/Data`; grep `extends Form`.
23. Dependency acquisition: constructor/action injection vs `FactoryLocator` / locator lookups.
    - Hint: grep `FactoryLocator`, `getTableLocator`, `fetchTable(` vs promoted constructor deps.
24. Decoupling: Events + listeners vs direct service/Table calls.
    - Hint: `ls src/Event src/Listener`; grep `EventManager`, `dispatch(`.
25. Configure / facade idiom: `Configure::read` vs injected config objects vs `env()` everywhere.
    - Hint: ratio of `Configure::` vs `env(` across `src/`.
26. Namespace layout (architecture): default `src/` skeleton vs domain/plugin folders.
    - Hint: `ls src/ plugins/`; look for Domain/, Modules/, bounded-context folders.
27. Enums: backed vs pure; case naming; where they live.
    - Hint: `ls src/**/Enum*`; grep `enum .*: string`, `enum .*: int`.

## F. Frontend & views

